    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d902">

                <pb facs="1703" n="1663" xml:id="pg1663"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">674.84A/10—454: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 902<lb/>The Ambassador in Egypt (Caffery) to the Department of State
                        <anchor n="1" xml:id="d902-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Cairo</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1954-10-04T14:00:00+02:00">October 4, 1954—2 p.m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">Confidential</p>
                <p>451. I fully concur with four points Russell made to Eytan (Tel Aviv telegram
                        306)<anchor n="2" xml:id="d902-f2"/> re Gaza Strip border situation.
                    Following comments refer to his four points:</p>
                <p>1. All incidents of which Israel complains are in category of private marauding.
                    For example, at emergency meeting October 2, Egypt condemned in case of two
                    Israelis killed September 25 (Tel Aviv telegram 298)<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d902-f3"/> and Chairman abstained in case of tractor driver shot in
                    hand (Tel Aviv telegram 281)<note n="3" target="d902fn3">Not printed.</note>
                    whereas Israel condemned for mortar fire, on September 28, on Egyptian military
                    post.</p>
                <p>2. Egypt not only talks about desiring control infiltration but takes helpful
                    unilateral action such as withdrawal Palestinian battalion from front positions
                    and imposition curfew in Strip.</p>
                <p>3. Egypt allows UN observers move about freely anywhere in Strip even after
                    curfew and with or without accompanying Egyptians. Only control is requirement
                    permission enter or leave Strip after dark which permission readily and speedily
                    granted.</p>
                <p>4. According to her and Embassy’s own impression number of incidents along DL
                    recently actually less than average.</p>
                <p>Egyptians believe Israelis seeking inflate normal incidents in Gaza area with
                    object discrediting Egypt in connection Suez base settlement and US aid
                    negotiations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> Caffery </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
